---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import MCQuiz from '../../components/MCQuiz.astro';
---

<Layout title='"Sidekiq or Solid Queue?"' description="Practice card. A trade-off question disguised as a 'pick one' question. Drills how to articulate when each fits.">
  <article class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 space-y-6">
    <div>
      <a href="/practice" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-2 mb-6">
        <span>←</span> Back to Practice
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-ruby font-semibold mb-2">Practice · Interview · Card 4</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ruby-dark mb-4">"Sidekiq or Solid Queue?"</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">The right answer is "it depends," followed by a clear articulation of what it depends on. Pick the version that lands.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-8 space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-gray-500">🔍</span> The question
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">"For a new Rails 8 app, would you reach for Sidekiq or Solid Queue?" Which answer reads as senior?</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-8 space-y-6 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
        <MCQuiz
          options={[
            {
              label: 'A',
              text: '"Sidekiq. It\'s the industry standard."',
              explanation: 'A default without a reason. Sidekiq is excellent, but Solid Queue is the new default for Rails 8 apps with moderate throughput. Picking Sidekiq without naming why is leaving signal on the table.',
            },
            {
              label: 'B',
              text: '"Solid Queue for moderate throughput (low thousands of jobs/min) where the team prefers one fewer infrastructure dependency — Postgres handles everything. Sidekiq when you need very high throughput, complex workflows like batches and pipelines, or you already run Redis for other reasons. For a greenfield app under a few thousand jobs/min, I\'d default to Solid Queue."',
              explanation: 'Concrete throughput threshold, specific reasons in each direction, and a default for a clear scenario. The "I\'d default to" sentence is the close. This reads as someone who has actually made this choice on a real project.',
              correct: true,
            },
            {
              label: 'C',
              text: '"Solid Queue. Redis is dead."',
              explanation: 'Hyperbolic and incorrect. Redis is fine, widely used, and Sidekiq remains the right tool for many workloads. "X is dead" is rarely a senior-sounding answer.',
            },
            {
              label: 'D',
              text: '"They\'re basically the same; you can swap one for the other with a config change."',
              explanation: 'ActiveJob lets you swap, yes, but they\'re not the same. Sidekiq has push-based polling, Pro/Enterprise features (batches, rate limiting, unique jobs), Redis under it. Solid Queue has polling-based execution, Postgres under it. Different scaling characteristics, different ops profiles.',
            },
          ]}
          principle={`<p>Trade-off questions test calibration, not memorization. The shape that scores:</p><ul class="list-disc list-inside ml-4 space-y-1"><li>Name the dimension the choice turns on (throughput, ops complexity, existing infrastructure).</li><li>Give a concrete threshold or condition.</li><li>State your default for the most likely case.</li></ul><p>Bonus: be explicit about not having all the data. "If you tell me the expected throughput and what other infrastructure the team already runs, I can refine the answer." Senior engineers make decisions under uncertainty and say so.</p>`}
          theoryHref="/lessons/interview-modern-stack"
          theoryLabel="Interview · The Modern Rails Stack"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-between items-center pt-4">
      <a href="/lessons/practice-interview-n-plus-one" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors">← Card 3</a>
      <a href="/lessons/practice-interview-hotwire" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors">Card 5 →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
